# Per-finding suppressions for the secret scan.
#
# Fingerprints, NOT paths. Ignoring `tests/` wholesale would hide a real
# credential in the test suite forever; each line here pins one exact
# file:rule:line, so anything else in the same file still fails the gate — and
# if one of these lines moves, its fingerprint stops matching and the finding
# comes back for re-review rather than staying silently suppressed.
#
# All of these are deliberately-invalid tokens in negative auth tests that
# assert a bad bearer returns 401/403. Verified individually:
#   wrong-key / definitely-not-the-real-token / totally-fake-garbage-token /
#   fake-ssrf-attempt / fake-hijack-attempt
#
# Paths carry the /repo prefix because the scan runs against a bind mount at
# /repo (see git-update.sh) — fingerprints include the scanned path.
/repo/tests/test_mcp.sh:curl-auth-header:111
/repo/tests/test_hybrids3.sh:curl-auth-header:92
/repo/tests/test_piston.sh:curl-auth-header:36
/repo/tests/test_security.sh:curl-auth-header:34
/repo/tests/test_security.sh:curl-auth-header:49
/repo/tests/test_security.sh:curl-auth-header:223
/repo/tests/test_security.sh:curl-auth-header:260
